WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.270
No. 4 Division is moving to secure

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.900
<b>An Alliance Appears</b>

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:07.980
Hizamaru Akari and Michelle K. Davis, as planned.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.190
As such, we've received a request for help.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.410
Everything is currently proceeding to plan.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.490
We just need to eliminate 
anything that resists.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.350
The terraformars haven't 
made any moves, as of yet,

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.380
so there shouldn't be any interruptions to 
the mission if things continue this way.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.560
Good.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.380
Russia & Northern Europe No. 3 Division

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.240
We, No. 4 Division,

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.630
will respond to the request for help 
in order to strengthen our alliance.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:36.390
In order to avoid the mistake of going in 
straight-on, we will split into two squads.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.600
And, Alexander...

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.530
Yes.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.380
I have a different mission for you.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.030
<i>Akari and Michelle.</i>

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:23.660
<i>The Joint US-Japanese division, No. 2 Division, 
to which they're assigned, fell into a trap.</i>

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.950
<i>No. 4 Division betrayed them.</i>

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.280
<i>They planned meticulously,</i>

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.470
<i>and attempted to obtain their 
special bodies for themselves.</i>

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:37.520
<i>In order to stop them, the enraged captain,</i>

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:41.010
<i>Shokichi Komachi, stormed the enemy camp.</i>

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.310
Listen up!

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:52.900
I injected hornet venom 
into your leader here.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.860
<b>Surgery Base Asian Giant Hornet</b>

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.860
<b>Komachi Shokichi</b>

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:58.400
He can't move because he's in so much pain that he wishes he were dead.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.500
And at this rate,

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.990
he will die.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.770
He'll have gone blind from 
the venom in his eyes.

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:07.560
Gangrene will develop in his extremities.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:11.170
His organs, his cardiopulmonary system, 
will stop functioning and fail.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.130
He will die a slow and painful death.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.510
But there is an antidote.

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:18.320
This is my weapon.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.880
It's not the least bit useful for this mission,

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.490
and that's the reason my rank is as low as it is.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.970
But I finally found a place to use it.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:29.310
No. 4 Division, surrender now!

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.770
I've caught you, Hornet!

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.650
My compatriots, I ask you 
not to worry about me.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.660
Shoot his legs!

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:46.950
Roger that!

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:00.660
Human transformation.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.270
This was fun,

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:06.760
Captain.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:11.770
However, we will win this war.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.170
I see you're not used to betrayal.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:19.940
Look at how big of a plan 
we've constructed here.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:24.450
Don't you think it would have been better 
to assume everything is not as it seems?

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.380
Our M.A.R.S. Rankings, our history.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.950
Even our surgery bases.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:34.000
Of course we've considered our bases 
with respect to fighting other humans.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.690
My base is not the anaconda...

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:39.880
No way that would be true.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.270
My base is the blue-ringed octopus.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.160
<b>M.A.R.S. Ranking #44
Liu Yiwu</b>

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.160
<b>Surgery Base Blue-Ringed Octopus</b>

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:46.810
Its known to carry the toxin, tetrodotoxin, 
which can encourage healing.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:52.070
As a venom, just a single 
octopus can kill seven humans,

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:55.080
but it can also be used as a 
painkiller in the medical field.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:59.620
Your hornet venom was supposed 
to leave me reeling in pain?

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:03.440
I don't feel a single thing.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.750
Now...

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:10.780
I want the captain's wounds tended to. 
We're keeping him as a hostage.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.220
Hong-chan.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.500
Get me the first again.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.730
R-Right!

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.460
I'll get it done now. Right now.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.510
I don't have any worth as a hostage.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:21.920
What?

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:23.880
Huh...?

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:28.250
General Liu, it seems like 
they're running away.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:34.050
Who's on board?

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.270
I'm sorry. I don't know.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.100
The worst situation is if

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.540
Michelle and Akari are the only 
ones piloting Unit 1 and Unit 2.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:43.960
Correct?

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:47.150
There are plenty of ways to stop them.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:51.030
They know what they need to do.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:52.530
Get away.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.120
Regroup.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.720
Until they get a chance to reformulate...

00:05:57.770 --> 00:06:00.560
They're not coming back.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:04.170
No matter how much you broadcast my screams.

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:08.930
If you're willing to say that 
much, I imagine that's true.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:11.390
However, you don't have to pretend.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.540
If you're willing to help 
me with these negotiations,

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:22.110
I'd be obliged to spare your life, Captain.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.520
You always were the joker,

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:27.720
Liu-san.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.620
Yeah, that was a joke.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.160
I knew you'd say that.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:41.420
That's why it couldn't be 
anything more than a joke.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:54.130
Well, that was sure fast 
on your part, Bao-kun.

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:55.790
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:57.930
The captain said he wasn't 
worth taking hostage.

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:02.000
Also, while we were talking to him, 
our targets were getting further away.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:03.690
That's true.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:07.940
Our situation hasn't changed very much.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.980
Give Unit 1 our final warning.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.370
If they don't respond, 
we'll shoot down Unit 2.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:14.970
Huh?

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:15.620
Hm?

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:20.560
Bao-san, why did you use the 
fixed battery to shoot him?

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:21.620
Actually...

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:25.860
Aren't you supposed to shoot 
moving terraformars with that...?

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:27.500
Huh?

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:28.370
Hong!

00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:29.720
Don't breath it in!

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:31.290
It's a chemical weapon!

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:34.510
Damn it! When did they...

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:36.560
How long have we...

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:38.430
...been having this illusion?

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.890
General Liu!

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:42.850
Captain Komachi's corpse isn't there!

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:47.050
The problem isn't how long we've 
been having this illusion...

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.450
This density...

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:51.060
If Berke hadn't noticed, 
we'd have been in trouble.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.380
They're trying to kill us.

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:56.450
For them to come at us like this...

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:00.990
You know, there are soldiers 
here, other than us...

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:03.070
This gas is #10's weapon!

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.410
Russia, huh?

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.220
Hey, Ivan.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.710
<b>M.A.R.S. Ranking #11
 Sergei Seleznyov
Russia & Northern Europe No. 3 Division
Surgery Base Japanese Mountain Mole</b>

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:14.640
What do you think they're dreaming about?

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:17.130
<b>M.A.R.S. Ranking #10
Ivan Perepelkina
Russia & Northern Europe No. 3 Division
 Surgery Base Datura Metel</b>

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:23.420
Captain!

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:30.790
Thank you so much...

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:35.900
You don't need to thank us.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:38.300
Wait...

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:40.960
Huh?

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:43.580
There are compounds in here 
from the Datura metel.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:49.040
There are anesthetics in as well, 
so it should lessen the pain slightly.

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:50.730
Thank you.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:54.280
If I add too much, 
you'll start seeing weird things.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:59.080
It depends on the person, 
but for the most part, you space out.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:03.750
The ones that aren't thrashing about 
are having pleasant dreams, I imagine.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:05.360
A tunnel...

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:07.190
They dug a tunnel, huh?

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:08.630
How're the missiles?!

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:09.650
They're fine!

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.770
We're still locked on to Unit 1 and 2.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.130
This is bad, General.

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:16.260
If there's a tunnel here, then...

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:19.370
No, they shouldn't have any explosives.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.350
We'll need to worry about 
their numbers for now...

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:24.280
General, they're coming!

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.170
Zheng, fire one of those missiles over here!

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.380
But the anti-air shield is going to...

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.250
Hurry up!

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:30.260
Too late.

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:31.240
It's right there.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:31.960
Huh?

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.430
Take cover.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:37.780
It's nothing more than a 
limited-ranged defensive weapon.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:39.500
Now, this is war.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.220
If we can do anything we want...

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.600
Destroying is simple.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.470
I see.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:22.070
I guess it's the Chinese New Year.

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:31.120
It's nice to see you, my fellow allies.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.740
As of today, we're proud 
to announce that we're

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:43.090
the Russian Federation Space Army, 
allies of the US-Japanese forces.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.680
Prepare yourselves.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:53.960
<b>High Speed Evacuation Pod: 

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:01.510
Once we confirm Kanako heading 
towards No. 3 Division,

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.160
we're going to take off.

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:06.500
Meet up with No. 6 Division.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:07.680
No. 6 Division?

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.370
The squad leader is Joseph.

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:11.600
We're not going to be taken out this easily.

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:24.870
I didn't want to rely so heavily 
on Joseph, but there's no choice.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:29.830
It's begun.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.620
<i>They actually came for us...</i>

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:34.450
<i>Russia & Northern Europe No. 3 Division...</i>

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:37.920
I'm thinking about shooting 
some missiles at you.

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:39.840
Then what should we do?!

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:44.600
If they're after Michelle and me, 
then they won't let us get away.

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:48.430
They're working on loading weapons.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.900
We can't get close to them or run.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:52.210
We call reinforcements.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:53.100
Reinforcements?

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:57.220
If you mean No. 3 Division it won't work.

00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:59.990
There's no reason for them join up with us.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:04.640
I imagine No. 3 Division is closer in 
terms of an alliance to No. 4 Division,

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:07.200
but that might just change.

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:09.320
What's happening on Earth then, huh?

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:10.060
Kanako.

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:10.790
Yes.

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:12.880
I'll buy us time.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:16.550
I want you to use that time to request 
help from the approaching No. 3 Division.

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:21.020
<i>They came, Captain.</i>

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:25.090
That mask isn't very fair.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:28.340
Without it, we would have won 
this already, my Ivan's gas would

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:30.600
have settled all this already.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:34.660
It seems your left foot has healed since 
you're wearing nothing on it like that.

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:37.360
If your base was an anaconda, 
you wouldn't be able heal.

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:40.250
Ivan's gas has already dissipated,

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:43.570
but he's still wearing a mask over 
there—he must be a crustacean-type.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:50.170
And the fact that he can't take off his mask 
means that you're releasing hapalotoxin.

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:51.980
Phew.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:55.100
In order to prey upon crustaceans, 
where tetrodotoxin is ineffective,

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:58.400
you can carry another toxin 
which is effective, hapalotoxin.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:12:59.750
In other words...

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:03.800
Your base is obviously a blue-ringed octopus.

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:07.590
And your base is a crab, a crustacean.

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:10.120
<i>The Tasmanian giant crab.</i>

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:10.300
Tasmanian Giant Crab

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:13.600
And I'd be in some serious trouble if I 
sat here chatting with you, however...

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:18.700
All I have to do to avoid the problem is this.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:22.550
I'd don't want to do this 
because I'd like to, but...

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.990
You're the guys who...

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:30.280
Sir, only Unit 4 has a false 
landing position reported.

00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:31.950
This is...

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:36.290
They taught the bugs that much...

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:39.230
...started this war!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.380
Voice Command: Bao.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:54.450
Fire on manual!

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.400
Damn.

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:20.180
No way.

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:23.170
Crustaceans are just thicker than we are.

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:25.170
What is he made of?

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.310
Damn kids!

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:55.850
One of those could have got in my eyes!

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:58.100
<b>Sylvester Asimov
Surgery Base Tasmanian Giant Crab
Mars Raking #3</b>

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:01.380
Monster...

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:04.040
Russian Army,

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:07.030
why did you change sides?

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:35.340
Our first goal is to capture Hizamaru Akari.

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:39.270
He was made to have a mosaic organ.

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:41.830
As a back up, we get Michelle K. Davis.

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:47.490
In order to understand that technology, 
we must check their bodies.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:51.630
I thought Russia was after the same thing.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:55.600
That's why we had you help 
in getting to Plan Delta.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:59.100
Our goal hasn't changed at all.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:02.680
We're here to eradicate 
the A.E. virus on Earth.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:07.700
At the very least, I think it's 
best for you to help us in

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:10.900
our initial plan to capture Hizamaru-kun.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:16.360
5 Days Ago: Earth, U-NASA Conference Room

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:20.560
I think we should take the lead 
in rescuing those on Mars.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:24.790
We already have a rescue ship ready 
loaded with tactical weapons.

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:29.400
Of course, we would continue 
Annex 1's mission.

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:32.220
<i>Not yet, Shichisei?</i>

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:34.700
Meanwhile: Japan, Saitama Prefecture Azaura City

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:40.980
Hyuga-kun, Someya-kun, get him in the car.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:42.670
Shichisei-san.

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:44.180
Who are they?

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:46.300
Russians, I believe.

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:47.150
I see.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:49.110
That was close.

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:53.650
All of the independent nations' research 
labs have had poor efficiency.

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:57.900
I believe it would be prudent to 
establish a joint organization.

00:16:57.900 --> 00:16:59.370
What do you think?

00:17:03.610 --> 00:17:04.850
Shichisei?

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:05.830
Yeah.

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:09.020
I see. Well done.

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:10.800
Could I have you put him on?

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:13.430
It's been awhile, Professor.

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:15.390
Thank you for everything.

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:16.510
Goodbye.

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:20.160
My country would provide the 
funds and the facilities.

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:21.840
Each country could...

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.810
We've secured Honda Ko.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:30.110
Wh-What was that, Hiruma-san?!

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:34.180
Professor Honda.

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:35.950
The one that created Hizamaru Akari.

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.520
That can't be!

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:42.320
I heard that Professor Honda 
was killed twenty years ago.

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.520
I just talked to him myself.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:46.330
He seemed fine to me.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.170
That's all I had to say.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:55.090
I'm sorry for interrupting.

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:56.280
Wait.

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:58.930
Is that all?

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:01.200
I see.

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:03.270
The information seems true.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:07.480
Things are always changing.

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:12.980
As long as you're taking the Annex as a 
stronghold, there's no way we can be allies.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.420
I don't care what happens on Earth.

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:19.830
If you side with US-Japan, 
we're not holding back.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:25.350
You're sounding pretty 
arrogant saying all of that,

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:28.000
but I think all of your wonderful 
weapons have been smashed.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:31.120
Guns don't have an effect on you.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:34.920
If we're going to do this, I'll fight you.

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:38.050
Do you know whose subordinates you killed?!

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:41.170
Give the traitors Sign A!

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:43.640
We're getting the Annex 
research facility back!

00:18:43.870 --> 00:18:44.800
Da!

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:47.290
Here we go, Kenpo guy!

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:51.770
Bring it on, 100-dan Judo man!

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:53.690
It's 7th dan!

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:56.610
Let the bosses fight each other!

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.150
I won't let anyone interfere!

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:01.650
Crabs get fed to octopuses.

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:04.790
Don't bring Earth's politics to Mars!

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:29.310
<i>A crustacean? A beetle?</i>

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:31.730
<i>No, some type of centipede or something?</i>

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:33.470
Oh?

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:34.910
Oh!

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:37.360
<i>This guy's shell will nullify 
any simple type of strike.</i>

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:39.250
<i>But the joints are vulnerable.</i>

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:41.780
<i>Or I can just wait for the 
toxin to take effect.</i>

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:46.660
<i>Any strike or attack against 
the joints won't work.</i>

00:19:47.190 --> 00:19:51.480
<i>However, any constriction or hits 
against the spinal cord will.</i>

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:00.170
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.580
<i>He's doing better than I expected.</i>

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:06.410
<i>At this rate, my endurance will 
run out before the toxin takes effect.</i>

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:16.410
Time to prey!

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:18.400
<b>Prey!!!</b>

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:23.260
<i>Foam?</i>

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:29.410
<i>I'm on his back?</i>

00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:34.000
<i>His mass...</i>

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:35.710
<i>It fell?</i>

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:04.880
I destroyed your semicircular canals.

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:07.320
Just lay down and pretend you can't fight.

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:13.910
Fa jin, huh?

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:19.080
It seems you thought that we were 
all engineers, reliant on weapons.

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:21.970
You came here and betrayed us.

00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:25.470
The only reason why we didn't and 
haven't surrendered, even though

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:28.140
we lost the alliance with 
you, No. 3 Division,

00:21:28.630 --> 00:21:30.390
is because we can win on our own.

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:33.700
Aaron!

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:34.790
Nina!

00:21:39.410 --> 00:21:40.900
What's wrong?

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.820
You seem to be having some issues.

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:51.000
It'll be fine, Papa.

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:54.290
You traitors!

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:56.960
You're the ones who betrayed us.

00:21:57.670 --> 00:22:01.840
You've betrayed mankind!

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
Three-way
